<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIAN FREIGHTER SINKS IN BLACK SEA.</title>
<headline>BULGARIAN FREIGHTER SINKS IN BLACK SEA.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian freighter Balkan Star 2 has sunk north of Varna off the Cape of Kaliakra, the head of the Varna Maritime Administration Nikola Simeonov told Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>He said the freighter listed to one side then sank suddenly but the circumstances of the accident were unclear.</p>
<p>Eight of the Bulgarian crew were rescued by a passing Cypriot ship and Bulgarian rescuers are searching for the ninth, he said.</p>
<p>The St Vincent and Grenadines-flagged freighter is owned by Sofia-based Balkan Machinery Holding.</p>
<p>-- Sofia newsroom 3592 84561</p>
